'''accent''' (ak-sent′), ''v. t.'' [< F. ''accenter'' = It. ''accentare''; from the noun. Cf. ''accentuate''.] '''1.''' To express the accent of; pronounce or utter with a particular stress or modulation of the voice: as, to ''accent'' a word properly.—'''2.''' To give expression to; utter.
{{smaller block|Congeal’d with grief, can scarce implore
Strength to ''accent'', Here my Albertus lies. {{right|''W. Wotton.''}}}}
'''3.''' To mark with a written accent or accents: as, to ''accent'' a word in order to indicate its pronunciation.—'''4.''' To emphasize; dwell upon; accentuate (which see).—{{smaller|'''Accented letter,''' in ''printing,'' a letter marked with an accent. See ''accent'', ''n.'', 3.—'''Accented parts of a bar,''' in ''music,'' those parts of the bar on which the stress falls, as the first and third}}

